  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.25.0 release assets and hashed independently. v5.25.0 replaces the SDD sub-agent delegation prohibition with a criterion the sub-agent applies itself: three gates (a tool that already compresses, independence of the parts, at least two of them) and two decisions (classify the deliverable's compression, pre-commit to the children's output schema). It adds `pegasus-general`, a generic worker with no phase contract, so a fan-out has a target that cannot collide with a phase result -- and that also removes `explore` and `general`, OpenCode built-ins the orchestrator used to name, from the allowlist, so every declared delegation target is now an agent Pegasus actually ships. DARQ inherits all of it renamed: the new agent installs as `darq-general`. Only the `pegasus` artifact changed; install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.23.0."
  }
